ac/old
ac/old2
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
*.png
# ...except the committed kittest reference snapshots (the A3 pixel
# regression equipment). The .old/.diff working files stay ignored.
!ac-rs/crates/ac-view/tests/snapshots/*.png
ac-rs/crates/ac-view/tests/snapshots/*.old.png
ac-rs/crates/ac-view/tests/snapshots/*.diff.png
*.csv

# Rig evidence — .json.gz / .pkl.gz frame captures and the .py that produced
# them — is COMMITTED, deliberately, under audit/<session>/. Same reasoning as
# the snapshot carve-out above: it is equipment, not output. A capture is the
# only record of what the instrument saw at a position that no longer exists,
# and analysis of it is re-run months later (audit/rig-session-3/ is 39 such
# files). Do not add a blanket *.json.gz / *.pkl.gz ignore — that omission is
# why several sessions' evidence sat untracked and invisible from a clone
# while the documents citing it were committed.
.env
*.key
*.pem
.vscode/
.idea/
pytest-of-mui/
stddocs
/.cargo/
.claude/CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json
work/sessions/
